xchange at 22:51:35 — about 90s after EVE considered the domain \"RUNNING\" — meaning the guest OS itself was still booting (kernel/USB enumeration/cloud-init) well past that point. A connection finally succeeded at 22:52:01, but the script execution over it returned `EOF`, consistent with the guest's sshd/network still settling under load, and the `Eventually` block's 180s deadline (from 22:50:04) expired at 22:53:04 before a stable session could be established. The DNAT/portmap rules and qemu process are confirmed correctly configured right now, so this looks like guest-boot/SSH-readiness flakiness (plausibly aggravated by nested-KVM boot jitter and/or the added complexity of enumerating the 4-deep USB hub chain inside the guest) rather than a config or reconciler bug. This exact test/symptom doesn't appear in the ledger, so it's a new failure, not a known recurring one.","time":{"start":1793916866000,"stop":1793917939840,"duration":1073840}},{"uid":"acaebc8d65b48dda","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/8/#testresult/acaebc8d65b48dda","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793836924000,"stop":1793837274300,"duration":350300}},{"uid":"f9228c472d6bf92a","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/7/#testresult/f9228c472d6bf92a","status":"passed","time":{"start":1793745535000,"stop":1793745807050,"duration":272050}}]},"tags":[]},"source":"2adf6061a3d5ded6.json","parameterValues":[]}